{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Bullish Spikes: The model consistently fails to capture rapid upward momentum (e.g., Nov 2022 surge from ~76 to ~89), forecasting only linear, low-magnitude increases. When sentiment history shows consecutive high values (1.00) or a sharp rise in sentiment, apply a significant upward bias correction to the forecast trajectory.",
    "Lag in Trend Reversal: The model exhibits a delayed reaction to trend changes, often continuing to forecast upward movement immediately after a peak or failing to anticipate the start of a downtrend. When sentiment drops from high (1.00) to low (0.00) or negative, immediately reduce the forecast slope to reflect mean reversion rather than gradual decay.",
    "Overconfidence in Mean Reversion: In volatile regimes (e.g., Dec 2023), the model assumes a slow return to the mean (68-70 range) while actual prices exhibit sharp volatility and deeper corrections (dropping to ~62). Do not rely on the model's flat, converging forecasts during high-volatility periods; instead, widen the forecast range to account for larger deviations.",
    "Horizon-Specific Decay: The model's 30-day forecast decays too slowly after a spike. If the true outcome shows a sharp drop following a peak, truncate the model's long-term tail to prevent overestimation in the 15-30 day horizon.",
    "Sentiment-Weighted Adjustment: When sentiment history averages above 0.67, the model's linear projection is insufficient; apply a non-linear multiplier to the first 5-10 days of the forecast to capture the initial explosive growth phase."
  ]
}
